{
  "description": "Language-agnostic laws of the brep.topology widgets. Component counts are the Euler counts of the primitives (a box has 8 vertices, 12 edges, 6 faces and one shell); lists are described by count plus a description every item satisfies. Selections name edges by their end points and faces by their planar outward normal, resolved to persistent labels of the input value; conversions and healing keep the analytic volume, area and bounds.",
